after about a day of deliberations in a  wrongful death lawsuit against republic  services this morning a jury found the  driver julio cortez solano negligent in  the death of an 11-year-old las vegas  girl good afternoon thank you for  joining us at 4 i'm kirstjen joyce and  i'm christian casadas victoria saha  joins us live with the details of the  verdict and how a grieving mother plans  to move forward victoria  jasmine espana was only 11 years old  when she was trying to cross the  sidewalk here sorry the crosswalk here  at viking and sand hill road and while a  driver from republic services was also  trying to cross that driver failed to  yield and a jury today found that  jasmine was also at fault  jasmine's mom and consonant espana  filed a wrongful death suit against  republic services her attorney asked for  65 million dollars in damages after a  two-week trial and almost two days of  deliberation the jury awarded her 38.8  million dollars jurors found republican  services driver julio cortes solano to  be negligent in jasmine's death they  also found jasmine partly to blame as  she entered the crosswalk without  looking where public services was found  negligent in hiring training and  retaining cortes solano jasmine's mother  said through a translator she hopes this  is the start of change for the company  and she says that she forgave him  the attorney for the espana family  wanted the driver to pay punitive  damages but the jury decided against it  i did reach out to republican services  regarding the verdict they sent a  statement saying quote we extend our  heart filled condolences to family and  friends of jasmine espana this was a  tragic accident republic services has  always maintained a strong culture  committed to safety and best in class  safety programs and will continue to do  so they also say they are unable to  comment further on  litigation excuse me reporting live  victoria saha 8 news now
 

